<https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_solutions> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "one earth solutions"@en ;
    dcterms:created "2026-11-11"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:creator "Michael DeBellis"@en ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/> ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-11-11"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:rights "Names, classification, and source links are attributed to One Earth. The ontology structure and concise draft descriptions were prepared for Common Action. This is not an official One Earth ontology. The license follows the existing One Earth project repository."@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.oneearth.org/categories/>,
        <https://www.oneearth.org/solutions/> ;
    dcterms:title "one_earth_solutions"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Direct hierarchy links are explicitly asserted in both directions for use without inference. The transitive has_subcategory and is_subcategory_of relations support ancestor queries when reasoning is enabled. Without reasoning, use a SPARQL property path over is_direct_subcategory_of. Themes and levers are kept outside the solution hierarchy; no solution-to-theme or solution-to-lever assignments are asserted."@en,
        "The ontology is standalone and has no imports. It reuses skos:Concept and SKOS documentation annotations, with the necessary term declarations included. It does not include the process model, Big Bro, or bioregion geometries. It can be loaded alongside other ontologies without adding those dependencies."@en,
        "This first draft represents categories as named individuals, not as executable processes or particular projects. It contains 3 pillars, 12 subpillars, 76 solution categories, 7 intersectional themes, and 7 levers of change. The main One Earth framework page determines membership and hierarchy. Definitions are short editorial descriptions for this draft, not quotations or official One Earth definitions."@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.1.0 - first draft for review"@en ;
    skos:definition "A lightweight Common Action ontology of One Earth solution categories, their hierarchy, intersectional themes, and levers of change."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Source snapshot reviewed on 2026-11-11. The Renewable Power category page additionally lists Advanced Nuclear, which is absent from the main framework page. It is not included in the 76-solution draft pending reconciliation."@en .

[] a owl:AllDisjointClasses ;
    owl:members ( oes:Pillar oes:Subpillar oes:Solution ) .

[] a owl:AllDisjointClasses ;
    owl:members ( oes:Solution_Category oes:Intersectional_Theme oes:Lever_Of_Change ) .

